  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-codex",
      "text": "English | [日本語](./README.ja.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Install the plugin from a DeepSeek Harness checkout:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh plugin --profile web add github:askdkc/dsh-codex\n```\n\nReplace `web` with the target profile name, then restart that profile.\n\nFor ACP, install the plugin in the ACP profile too:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh plugin --profile acp add github:askdkc/dsh-codex\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Profiles load plugins independently: installing into `web` does not add models to `acp`. Restart the DSH process launched by your ACP client, then reopen its model selector. If the client uses a different profile, replace `acp` with that name."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "This plugin ships prebuilt `lib` files and does not need install-time build scripts. If an installation or update fails with `ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS` naming `codex-subscription-oauth-plugin`, edit the target profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (by default, `~/.dsh/profiles/web/pnpm-workspace.yaml`). In its existing `allowBuilds` map, explicitly skip this package's build scripts:\n\n```yaml\nallowBuilds:\n  codex-subscription-oauth-plugin: false\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Change an existing `codex-subscription-oauth-plugin: true` to `false`. Delete any other `allowBuilds` entries whose key starts with `codex-subscription-oauth-plugin@`, including repository URLs, commit URLs, and generated `set this to true or false` placeholders. Keep only the name-only `false` entry for this package and preserve other packages' settings. Save the profile file before retrying."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Unlike a name-only `true`, a name-only `false` also applies to Git dependencies: pnpm records an explicit decision to skip the scripts, so updates do not require commit-hash edits. This recovery works with pnpm 11.7.0; upgrading pnpm is not required. See pnpm's [Git dependency build settings](https://pnpm.io/settings/build#allowbuilds)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Then rerun the failed `pnpm dsh plugin ...` command from the DeepSeek Harness checkout. Even an update of another plugin checks this profile's dependencies; for example, retry a failed Kiokuko update with:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh plugin --profile web update kiokuko-dsh --latest\n```\n\nWait for the command to exit successfully. `Already up to date` can appear before a build-policy error and does not by itself mean the update succeeded."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Use the same profile for the configuration edit and retry; adjust the path for a custom `DSH_HOME`. Running `pnpm approve-builds` in the Harness checkout targets that checkout, not the plugin profile. Changing `minimumReleaseAge` does not resolve build approval failures.\n\nIf installation into an existing ACP profile fails with `ERR_PNPM_UNEXPECTED_STORE`, reinstall that profile's dependencies using the current pnpm store, then retry:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm --dir ~/.dsh/profiles/acp install --force --frozen-lockfile\npnpm dsh plugin --profile acp add github:askdkc/dsh-codex\n```\n\nThe first command rebuilds the profile's `node_modules` without changing its lockfile. If it fails, resolve that error before retrying the plugin installation. If you use a custom `DSH_HOME` or profile name, adjust both commands. The `allowBuilds` hint printed after a store mismatch does not fix this error.\n\nSign in to ChatGPT for Codex:\n\n```text\n/codex-auth\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Complete the browser login. If the localhost callback cannot reach DSH, paste the redirect URL or authorization code when prompted.\n\nRemove the plugin:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh plugin --profile web remove codex-subscription-oauth-plugin\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Models and connection diagnostics",
      "text": "The plugin bundles the pi-ai 1.5.0 Codex catalog, so every model the authenticated Codex endpoint currently lists as visible has executable metadata without a manual model table: GPT-5.6 Luna, Sol, and Terra; GPT-6 Astra, Luna, and Sol; and GPT-6.1 Sol and Terra. Account visibility and ordering still come from the authenticated catalog at `https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/models`; an account that cannot see a model does not receive it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Models and connection diagnostics",
      "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol and Terra use the Codex default 500,000-token context, 128,000-token output capacity, text and image input, and the reasoning levels recorded in the catalog. Their prices come from the OpenAI API model pages. Unknown entries that the live endpoint lists but the bundled catalog cannot execute emit `MODEL_METADATA_MISSING` and stay hidden; their capabilities are not guessed from another model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Models and connection diagnostics",
      "text": "Connection failures retain the SDK's before/after-start phase, fallback choice and safe error code. Raw close reasons, stacks, headers and bodies are omitted from these diagnostics. The SDK may switch to SSE before its first response event; the plugin adds no retries and does not replay an interrupted response or tool output. Cancellation stays cancelled, and an SSE HTTP error retains its status for the host's classification."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT. See [LICENSE](./LICENSE).\n\nBundled third-party notices are listed in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](./THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)."
    }
  ],
